  "can_do": "She can break anything by finding its natural frequency and hitting that note, while the formally trained singers are locked into predetermined ranges and lists. Her gift adapts to the object instead of forcing it into a system.",
  "in_the_way": "Her voice. Every time she uses the gift it tears her throat, leaves her bleeding or voiceless for days — and in a world where everything runs on voice, losing yours is catastrophic. Also her precarious place: she's only tolerated because she can do what trained singers cannot, so pushing past that puts her outside the only system that would keep her.",
  "expect_next": "A progression story about a misfit learning to master an unconventional gift. I expect her to leave the singers' yard, probably by choice or by being cast out, and the book to track what it takes to reach that audience she wants — both in terms of her physical voice holding up and in navigating whatever system or gatekeeping exists in the wider world. There's going to be real cost.",
